cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use attestqa, please cite it as below. The DOI is the concept DOI and resolves to the latest archived version; a specific version has its own DOI on its Zenodo page."
type: software
title: "attestqa (formerly agentic-qa): governed agentic end-to-end testing"
abstract: >-
  A runtime for agentic software testing in which a language model proposes tool
  calls but decides nothing. Every proposed call is classified against a manifest
  and resolved by an operator-owned policy table into execute, ask, or refuse; an
  unclassified operation is refused by default. Completion is decided by code that
  reads the run's evidence rather than by the model's own account of itself. Each
  cycle is reassembled from an append-only JSONL ledger rather than from a
  conversation, so a run can be replayed offline and every reported figure traces
  to a recorded event. The reference skill turns a user story's acceptance criteria
  into executable Playwright tests and records the resulting test cases against the
  story in Jira or Azure DevOps.
